<item>
            <title>[MAHOUT-1063] ARFF parser does not support &apos;integer&apos; and &apos;real&apos; attribute types</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MAHOUT-1063</link>
                <project id="12310751" key="MAHOUT">Mahout</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;ARFF format supports attributes specified as &apos;integer&apos; and &apos;real&apos;. They are treated just like &apos;numeric&apos;:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://weka.wikispaces.com/ARFF+%28stable+version%29&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://weka.wikispaces.com/ARFF+%28stable+version%29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Latest Weka development versions come with examples using these types.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12605854">MAHOUT-1063</key>
            <summary>ARFF parser does not support &apos;integer&apos; and &apos;real&apos; attribute types</summary>
